# Every text file is LF, in the repo and when checked out, whatever a
# machine's core.autocrlf says. The tools write LF (.editorconfig, Vitest's
# snapshots, the generators), and tests compare files' text, so a checkout in
# CRLF made changes that weren't there, and failures that only happened on
# Windows. Git tells binary files apart, and leaves them as they are.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Written by packages/libraries/utils/scripts/generate-refresh-copies.ts. GitHub collapses
# it in diffs and leaves it out of the language statistics.
packages/libraries/utils/src/jsx/refresh-copies.ts linguist-generated=true
